#: tmpl/overview.php:32 tmpl/topbar.php:39
msgid "Help"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:33
msgid ""
"Quick walkthroughs of what Repuso does and how to get the most out of it."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:43
msgid "Where do I find my widget shortcode?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:44
msgid ""
"Open the Widgets tab in this plugin. Each widget row shows its shortcode "
"(like [rw_grid id=\"123\"]). Click it to copy. Paste into any WordPress "
"page, post, or block to embed."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:47
msgid ""
"Why are my reviews not appearing on the page after I added the shortcode?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:48
msgid ""
"Most often this is a caching plugin holding the page contents. Clear your "
"site cache and reload. Also check that the widget on Repuso has at least one "
"approved review and a connected channel. Some widget types only render once "
"the underlying script loads in the browser - if your theme strips scripts on "
"certain pages, switch the widget to a different layout."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:51
msgid "How do I connect a new review channel (Google, Facebook, etc.)?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:52
msgid ""
"Use the Channels tab inside the plugin to see what is already connected. To "
"add a new one, click \"Connect a channel\" to open the Repuso dashboard - "
"new channels are added from there. Once added, reviews start flowing back "
"into your widgets automatically."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:55
msgid "How long until reviews appear after I connect a channel?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:56
msgid ""
"Usually a matter of minutes, but it can take up to 24 hours depending on the "
"channel and how many reviews are being imported. After the initial fetch, "
"Repuso checks for new reviews automatically on a regular schedule."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:59
msgid "Are new reviews pulled in automatically?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:60
msgid ""
"Yes. Once a channel is connected, Repuso monitors it for new reviews and "
"pulls them in automatically as soon as they appear publicly on the source. "
"New reviews can take up to 24 hours to populate, depending on when the "
"channel was last checked and how the source surfaces them. If the channel is "
"set to auto-approve 4 and 5 star ratings, new high-rated reviews are also "
"displayed in your widgets straight away with no manual approval needed. "
"Lower-rated reviews stay in the Inbox waiting for your approval."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:63
msgid "Why are some reviews not showing in my widget?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:64
msgid ""
"Open the Reviews tab in the plugin. Anything in the Inbox is pending "
"approval and will not display in widgets until you approve it. Reviews you "
"dismissed are hidden by design. Approved reviews appear in widgets within a "
"few seconds (your widget may also have its own filters like minimum star "
"rating)."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:67
msgid "How do I customize how my widgets look?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:68
msgid ""
"Each widget has a designer in the Repuso dashboard - click Edit on the "
"widget row in the Widgets tab to open it. You can change colors, fonts, "
"layout, density, and more without touching code. On the Standard and "
"Ultimate plans you can also add Custom CSS for fine-grained tweaks."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:71
msgid "Can the same widget be used on multiple WordPress sites?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:72
msgid ""
"Yes. A widget shortcode can be embedded on as many pages and sites as you "
"want - reviews and widget settings update centrally from Repuso, so a change "
"applies everywhere instantly."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:75
msgid "How do I show the floating widget only on certain pages?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:76
msgid ""
"Open the Widgets → Floating widget tab. There you can pick the widget to "
"use, restrict it to specific WordPress content types, exclude individual "
"pages, and add Show/Hide rules by URL pattern."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:79
msgid "How do I switch between sub-accounts?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:80
msgid ""
"Use the account dropdown on the right side of the top bar inside the plugin. "
"The dropdown only shows when you have more than one sub-account on Repuso. "
"Switching there updates the data shown on every plugin page (Dashboard, "
"Reviews, Channels, Widgets)."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:83
msgid "Do you offer a free trial?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:84
msgid ""
"Yes - 10 days, fully functional, no credit card needed. Start it from repuso."
"com."
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:87
msgid "Can I cancel my subscription?"
msgstr ""

#: tmpl/overview.php:88
msgid ""
"Yes, anytime. Your subscription will not renew. If you have paid and changed "
"your mind within 7 days of payment, we will issue a full refund."
msgstr ""

